  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/astatheros-macracanthus-formerly-cichlasoma-m/",
      "html": "<p>Astatheros macracanthus (formerly Cichlasoma macracanthus) is a cichlid 20-25 cm long. It was scientifically described in 1864 but has always remained a rarity in the aquarium. In normal coloration it is pretty but not striking; during breeding the parents are almost snow-white with contrasting, pitch-black lateral markings on the hind body and pitch-black lips.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/astatheros-macracanthus-formerly-cichlasoma-m/",
      "html": "<p>The species is distributed quite widely from southern North America to Guatemala and El Salvador.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/astatheros-macracanthus-formerly-cichlasoma-m/",
      "html": "<p>The care of these typical open-breeders with parental care corresponds to that of all Central Americans of the same robust type: aquaria as large as possible dampen the aggressiveness. Strong filtering provides hygienic conditions.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/astatheros-macracanthus-formerly-cichlasoma-m/",
      "html": "<p>The water values are of secondary importance, if extremes are avoided.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/astatheros-macracanthus-formerly-cichlasoma-m/",
      "html": "<p>Sand, stones and roots form the main furnishings.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/astatheros-macracanthus-formerly-cichlasoma-m/",
      "html": "<p>Varied nutrition: almost everything that fits into the mouth is eaten, while vegetable components are usually hardly touched.</p>"
    }
  ],
